- DISEMBARK: the player exits or transfers out of the vehicle.

A vehicle moving or reaching its scheduled destination is not player movement. If the player remains aboard, answer NONE even when the vehicle arrives, its doors open, or destination scenery appears in the draft. Do not turn an unauthorized draft disembarkation into game state: respect explicit <playerAction> constraints and remove the mistaken departure from final prose.
Do not answer DESTINATION while the player is aboard; leaving the vehicle is DISEMBARK.
